{
  "$comment": "What makes two geniuses of the same form look unlike each other, and what the player may choose. Born variation is drawn from the genius's identity (its partner's Seed, Pattern, spark and name: game/scripts/genius/genius_look.gd) and is stable for life: a coat out of its body's palette, which of its body's marking regions show, its proportions, how its light burns. The player chooses among a few coats (born.coatsOffered, the born one first), turns markings on and off, and gives it a keepsake. Colours follow the art bible: the partner's Shape colour is the one loud colour, so every coat here is a muted earth, stone or metal. bodies: per silhouette. roles maps the body's material names to a role (main, under, trim); marks names its marking regions (materials called mark_<region> in the art; 'on' is the role whose colour hides the marking when it is off); coats names a palette; shapes lists which proportions it carries as blend shapes (the rest fall back to a scale of the whole body, proportions[].scale). A body not listed here keeps the colours it was made in.",
